63. Multiple changes + SAVEPOINT + undo later change + COMMIT

This combines everything.

START TRANSACTION;

UPDATE sales_orders
SET price = 1300
WHERE order_id = 2;

UPDATE sales_orders
SET price = 9000
WHERE order_id = 3;

SAVEPOINT correct_changes;

UPDATE sales_orders
SET price = -500
WHERE order_id = 4;

SELECT order_id, price
FROM sales_orders
WHERE order_id IN (2, 3, 4);

ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT correct_changes;

COMMIT;

Result:

Order 2 → saved
Order 3 → saved
Order 4 → incorrect update undone

This is basically the full TCL pattern:

START TRANSACTION
       ↓
  Correct changes
       ↓
   SAVEPOINT
       ↓
  Wrong change
       ↓
ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT
       ↓
    COMMIT